# Courtemanche-Ramirez-Nattel (1998) human atrial myocyte model.
#
# UNITS: this deck's clock is in ms and its currents are ABSOLUTE, so
# the stimulus amplitude below is in pA (-2000 pA = -2 nA), not the
# pA/pF density a TTP deck uses.  The CEP models do not share a unit
# system -- do not copy stimulus blocks or time steps between decks.
# Table: ../README_CEP_UNITS.md
#
# The protocol below reproduces the paper's Figs. 14/15 beat: 2-ms,
# -2 nA (twice diastolic threshold) pulses at a period of 1000 ms.
# The paper reports the AP after 12 s of pacing from rest; this
# example runs a single 600-ms window from rest to keep the log small.
# For the full paper protocol set: Number of time steps: 2400000

Electrophysiology model: crn {
    CEP model parameters file path: params_crn.in
}

Time integration scheme: fe

Number of time steps: 120000

Time step size: 0.005     # ms

Stimulus: I {
    Amplitude: -2000.0    # pA (2 nA)
    Start time: 0.0       # ms
    Duration: 2.0         # ms
    Cycle length: 1000.0  # ms
}
